{"name":"Bread and Butter","hex":"#ffd182","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bread and butter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is central or fundamental, as to one's business, survival, or income; a staple or cornerstone.","The basic requirements of living, such as food and housing."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Said when two people walking together are temporarily separated by an obstacle in order to indicate that they belong together."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bread_and_butter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bread","blocks":[{"text":"Bread is a baked food product made from water, flour, and often yeast. It is a staple food across the world, particularly in Europe and the Middle East. Throughout recorded history and around the world, it has been an important part of many cultures' diets. It is one of the oldest human-made foods, having been of significance since the dawn of agriculture, and plays an essential role in both religious rituals and secular culture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG/330px-Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bread"},{"title":"Bread and Butter (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bread and Butter\" is a 1964 song by American pop vocal trio the Newbeats. Written by Larry Parks and Jay Turnbow, \"Bread and Butter\" was the group's first and most popular hit, reaching No. 2 on the US Billboard Hot 100."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/The-newbeats-bread-and-butter-hickory-5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bread_and_Butter_(song)"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG/500px-Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG/1280px-Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG/500px-Korb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKorb_mit_Br%C3%B6tchen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg/500px-Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg/1280px-Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg/500px-Woman_baking_bread-E_25213-IMG_4514-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woman baking bread (c. 2200 BC); Louvre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki